 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Hacia un lugar",
    "@en": "To a place"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**-a/-e** significa «a/hacia»: **okula** (a la escuela), **eve** (a casa), **bankaya** (al banco). Si el nombre acaba en vocal, se intercala **y**: **kafeye** (a la cafetería).",
     "@en": "**-a/-e** means «a / to»: **okula** (to school), **eve** (to home), **bankaya** (to bank). If the name ends in vowel, **y**: **kafeye** (to the cafeteria) is intercelled."
    },
    {
     "@es": "**Nereye?** = ¿adónde? **Nereden?** = ¿de dónde? Compara **okulda** (en la escuela), **okula** (a la escuela) y **okuldan** (desde la escuela).",
     "@en": "**Nereye?** = where? **Nereden?** = from where? Compare **okulda** (at school), **okula** (at school) and **okuldan** (from school)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Indicaciones",
    "@en": "Indications"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**Sağa dön** = gira a la derecha; **sola dön** = gira a la izquierda. **Düz git** = sigue recto. **Yakın** significa cerca y **uzak**, lejos.",
     "@en": "**Sağa dön** = turn right; **sola dön** = turn left. **Düz git** = is still straight. **Yakın** means near and **uzak**, far away."
    },
    {
     "@es": "**Buraya** = hacia aquí; **şuraya** = hacia allí (cerca del interlocutor).",
     "@en": "**Buraya** = here; **şuraya** = there (near the interlocutor)."
    }
   ]
  },
